The simplest way to reliably get confused in the late game is to forget
a useless spell, i.e., never to cast it, until it is expired. Then you
get confused each time you cast it, without using up any power. So you
do not need a single item. For poor spellcasters, high-level spells are
useless. Also, if you get the spell of knock or of wizard lock, they are
not too interesting once you are beyond the castle. Cure blindness is
another unimportant spell, as a blessed unicorn horn will do the job
anyway.





